# Nothing in this repo had a .gitignore anywhere (checked root and every sub-project) despite
# node_modules/ and target/ already existing as real build output, and .finora/installation.key
# holding a real bootstrap secret in the repo root -- all of that was one `git add .` away from
# being committed. This exists to close that gap; see the deployment-readiness discussion this
# was written alongside for the full context ("no production values should exist inside source
# code" applies just as much to what accidentally ends up in git history as to what's hardcoded
# in application.yml).

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BootstrapService writes a real one-time installation key here for local/dev setup (see
# RFC-BOOTSTRAP-01 in docs/bootstrap-setup-future-work.md) -- never committed, regardless of
# environment.
.finora/
*.env
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.development
.env.production
# The checked-in template is the one exception -- it never holds a real value.
!.env.example

# --- Java / Maven (backend/) --------------------------------------------------------------
backend/target/
*.class
*.jar
!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
hs_err_pid*.log

# --- Node / Vite (frontend/, admin-portal/) -------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.local
.vite/

# --- IDE / editor (kept minimal -- .vscode/settings.json here is shared team config, not
# per-developer, so it stays tracked; only ignore genuinely machine-specific IDE state) -------
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# --- OS ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Logs ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# --- Node / Vite ---
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
.vite/
*.local
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Cloudflare Wrangler ---
.wrangler/

# --- Maven ---
.mvn/timing.properties